<h1>Drake Warren</h1>
<p>Cook County Commissioner, 10th District, on the Chicago ballot November 3, 2026. Party: Democratic.</p>
<p><a href="https://drakefor10.com/" rel="nofollow noopener">Campaign site (drakefor10.com)</a></p>
<h2>Running on</h2>
<p>His campaign site lists six planks: protecting health care (strengthening Cook County Health and CountyCare), fairness in property taxes, lowering the cost of living by expanding housing supply, standing up to federal actions including immigration enforcement and data sharing, restorative justice, and an open and ethical county government. In coverage he has also proposed ethics rules barring officials from voting on matters tied to their employers and exploring land value or split-rate taxation.</p>
<h2>Background</h2>
<p>Industrial engineer and West Monroe consultant who spent about a decade as a community organizer on housing, health care access, and environmental restoration; a first-time candidate who served on the Chicago Growth Project steering committee.</p>
